(6427920, 952960, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by littlemav:</b></div><hr/><i> I couldn''t even grasp how you did this, Then after reading, I am still flabbergasted! Congratulations on a WELL DESERVED BLUE!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>When a frog sit on a small platform surrounded by water, it can not go anywhere but jump into water. A dropper was in my hand to create water drops and ripples. The whole background was water surface with reflections on it. No nature light played the role, only high speed flash can freeze this action in macro. I used <a href="//vahonen.com/photo/equipment/flashes/nissin/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Nissin 360 old fashion auto flash</a> which provide extreme high speed when set in auto mode and lowest output power.</td>', 'Originally posted by littlemav: I couldn''t even grasp how you did this, Then after reading, I am still flabbergasted! Congratulations on a WELL DESERVED BLUE!!  When a frog sit on a small platform surrounded by water, it can not go anywhere but jump into water. A dropper was in my hand to create water drops and ripples. The whole background was water surface with reflections on it. No nature light played the role, only high speed flash can freeze this action in macro. I used Nissin 360 old fashion auto flash which provide extreme high speed when set in auto mode and lowest output power.', '2011-05-30 02:22:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6427922, 952846, 90495, '<td valign="top">Great capture here. My only 10 vote. I see the 1,2,3 trolls were out again for this water drop. <br/> <br/>Did you add anything to your water like rinse-aid for dishwashers?</td>', 'Great capture here. My only 10 vote. I see the 1,2,3 trolls were out again for this water drop.  Did you add anything to your water like rinse-aid for dishwashers?', '2011-05-30 02:22:52.000000', NULL, 0),
