(6428366, 952846, 96751, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by enizmon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> That is one heck of a capture.  Breathtaking clarity, and that little water cap with fringes over the second drop is unreal. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The second drop is as is. I''ve done many shots of water drop collisions and something that I never do is manipulate the shapes of the collision of water droplets. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL!  That was a compliment, Enrique.  "Unreal" as in incredible, fabulous.  Not as in, I don''t believe it is possible to do this without manipulation :-)<br/> <br/>Felicidades!!</td>', 'Originally posted by enizmon: Originally posted by tanguera: That is one heck of a capture.  Breathtaking clarity, and that little water cap with fringes over the second drop is unreal.  The second drop is as is. I''ve done many shots of water drop collisions and something that I never do is manipulate the shapes of the collision of water droplets.   LOL!  That was a compliment, Enrique.  "Unreal" as in incredible, fabulous.  Not as in, I don''t believe it is possible to do this without manipulation :-) Felicidades!!', '2011-05-30 13:37:32.000000', NULL, 0),
